-- The self-hosted checker's entry point (stage 23e). The checker is the language
-- (`Lex`, `Parse`, `Kernel`, `CParse`, `CGlue`, `Frontend`) and the tables
-- (`selfhost/Tables.wiz`, generated); `moduleMain` reads `input.wiz`, resolves the
-- modules it imports under the `-I` roots (then the working directory), and prints what
-- the frontend makes of them.
--
-- It is a checked-in module like the others: `Wiz/Selfhost.checkerSource` concatenates
-- it last. It replaces the `def main := moduleMain cats tokens` string that the Lean
-- side used to write. The compiler's entry point is `selfhost/Main.wiz`.
def main : IO Unit := moduleMain cats tokens
